From 348c8db7855e18afcbcfd585dae497be91178dcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:39:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): priority migrate checks host-map
 coverage before staging; add read-only origins check

Run 1 of the f953 migrate (op bdc414c0) refused 'host map must exactly cover
manifest origins' only after the local writer had written its backup and
attachment, so every retry needed new paths, and the live origin set could be
read only by running migrate.

- migrate now captures the canonical manifest first, compares the explicit host
  map with the captured origins (missing/extra in the report) and refuses before
  stage() writes any backup or attachment; it then stages that same manifest.
- --priority-operation origins: read-only check printing {origins, missing,
  extra, errors}; exit 1 on a missing origin or unmapped/rowless writer. Same
  operator fence; refuses backup/task/manifest/attachment/digest/rollback flags.
- Superset maps: entries for origins owning no captured row are reported as
  skipped and never contacted. Missing entries still refuse. Hosts are never
  inferred.
- Runbook: a coverage mismatch consumes no backup path or attachment.
